# Shell scripts must keep LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# scripts/klar-entry.sh is COPY'd straight into the container image and run as
# the entrypoint. On a Windows checkout git converts it to CRLF, the shebang
# becomes `#!/bin/sh\r`, and the kernel fails to find an interpreter called
# `/bin/sh\r` — reported as "exec /usr/local/bin/klar-entry.sh: no such file
# or directory", which looks like the script is missing when it is not.
# A local `docker build` then produces an image that cannot start, while the
# same commit built in CI on Linux is fine.
*.sh text eol=lf
